  "paperwork": "Paperwork Paperwork MF-2409-117 · prepared by the Paperwork agent at the award The pack is drafted at the awardRakesh's tax invoice, the e-way bill check, Munchly's price-support credit note, the ITC memo, the FSSAI checklist and the destruction certificate, each generated or marked not required with the reason. Paperwork agentDrafts the whole pack once the lot is awarded and on the buyer's truck. ReportsEvidenceBatches ⟨Munchly Foods workspace, on Smart-Clearance | Notifications | Notifications | Profile and settings | Main⟩",
  "profile": "Profile Profile Sustainability & BRSR Vikram Sethi Sustainability & BRSR · Munchly FoodsGoogle Workspace · vikram.sethi@munchly.in Workspace Munchly Foodsmunchly.smartclearance.comMunchly staff Appearance ThemeLightDarkAuto Notifications LanguageEnglishहिन्दीPush notificationsWeekly digest by email Offers to the trade go out in the language each person picks. Account Switch personTry the journey as someone else in the story Reset demo dataPuts the batch back to the start Sign outBack to munchly.smartclearance.com ReportsEvidenceBatches ⟨Munchly Foods workspace, on Smart-Clearance | Notifications | Notifications | Profile and settings | Theme | Notification language | Push notifications | Weekly digest | Main⟩",
  "report": "Finance & ESG Finance & ESG Q3 FY27 · Oct to Dec 2026 · one ledger, two readings QuarterThis batch Recovered₹6.3 lakh₹60123456789.30123456789lakh GST credit protected₹79,000₹7012345678990123456789,001234567890012345678900123456789 Kept out of landfill5.750123456789.70123456789 t CO₂e avoided14.251012345678940123456789.2012345678950123456789 tindicative · 2.5 kg a kg Meals served3,70030123456789,701234567890012345678900123456789 A synthetic quarter: the totals are the walkthrough's; the weekly split, the channel mix and the BRSR split below are illustrative. Week 1 is this batch. Recovered against the would-be write-off Illustrative weekly split of the quarter RecoveredWould-be write-off 0₹35k₹70kW1W3W5W7W9W11W13 Channel mix Share of units by where they went · illustrative Kirana scheme: 42%ExpireSoon: 38%Staff sale: 5%Food bank: 12%Write-off: 3% Kirana scheme 42%ExpireSoon 38%Staff sale 5%Food bank 12%Write-off 3%How the tax maths works Destroying stock costs more than the stock. You lose it at cost, reverse the GST input credit under Section 17(5)(h), pay to dispose of it, and owe EPR on the product and pack. Selling it under a tax invoice keeps the credit. That is why every routed batch protects its ITC, even at half the MRP. Donations reverse it. Section 17(5)(h) blocks credit on gifts, and since 1 October 2023 section 17(5)(fa) blocks it on CSR donations too, so a food-bank route costs the credit on every pack. Disposal ₹1.50 a unit, indicativeEPR ₹6 a kg, indicativeCO₂e 2.5 kg per kg, indicative 5.7 tonnes kept out of landfill this quarter, with invoices behind every kilo. That goes straight into the annual report. Vikram · sustainability BRSR Core Principle 6, waste management · the quarter's 5.7 t, split illustrative Export BRSR table CategoryDiverted, kgResoldDonatedDisposedEvidenceFood waste: packaged food past quick-commerce gates4,8404,26058060Tax invoices, ExpireSoon listing IDs, in-app order logs, food-bank receiptsPlastic packaging (EPR)8607709010Packaging weights per SKU, EPR factor, the same invoices ReportsEvidenceBatches ⟨Munchly Foods workspace, on Smart-Clearance | Notifications | Notifications | Profile and settings | Period | Weekly recovered against would-be write-off | Channel mix | BRSR waste table | Main⟩",
}
`;

