  "paperwork": "Smart‑Clearance Munchly Foodsmunchly.smartclearance.com Finance & ESG Evidence Batches Vikram SethiSustainability & BRSR · Munchly Foods Paperwork Paperwork MF-2409-117 · prepared by the Paperwork agent at the award Rakesh's invoice₹11,510₹11,510 Price support₹8,768₹8,768 GST credit kept₹1,224₹1,224 Things to chase0 Document pack Generated, drafted or not required, each with its reason Exportreviewed drafted Tax invoice INV/26-27/0931 · Rakesh Traders ₹11,510₹11,510not required E-way bill check MF-2409-117 · Rakesh Traders ₹11,510₹11,510generated Price-support credit note CN/0117 · Munchly Foods ₹8,768₹8,768generated GST ITC memo s.17(5)(h) · Munchly Foods ₹1,224₹1,224not required FSSAI surplus-food checklist no donation · Munchly Foods Nothing to filenot required Destruction certificate 0 units left · Munchly Foods Nothing to file Who keeps what Rakesh Traders receives₹30,314 and paid 1,360 × ₹22, the van and the fee−₹30,314 He ends whole₹0 Expiry claim Munchly avoids₹34,490 Price support it pays instead−₹8,768 Better for Munchly₹25,722₹25,722 The same ₹25,722 swing as the ledger, seen from Munchly's cash: the ₹22 credit Rakesh would have claimed and the ₹22 he paid cancel out. At plan prices it is ₹8,150 of support and a ₹26,340 swing. Credit note, GST memo, and Rakesh's invoice attached as evidence. First batch this year with nothing for me to chase. Anita · finance Tax invoice Drafted for Rakesh Traders Tax invoice INV/26-27/0931 · draft · 5 Oct 2026 IGST FromRakesh TradersKalamna Market, Nagpur, MaharashtraGSTIN 27AABCR1234F1Z5 ToAgrawal WholesaleGanj Mandi, Raipur, Chhattisgarh · place of supply 22GSTIN 22AAGFA4821M1Z3 ItemHSNQtyRateTaxableMunchly Masala Chips 150 gBatch MF-2409-117 · best before 18 Nov 20262005772₹14.20₹10,962.40 Taxable value₹10,962.40IGST 5% Maharashtra → Chhattisgarh₹548.00Round off−₹0.40Invoice total₹11,510.00 Drafted by the Paperwork agent for Rakesh Traders to issue from Tally. Chips moved from 12% to 5% GST under GST 2.0 on 22 September 2025. The MRP of ₹30.00 stays printed on every pack: a discounted sale is fine, a second MRP is not (Legal Metrology). ⟨Main | Munchly Foods workspace, munchly.smartclearance.com | Vikram Sethi · Sustainability & BRSR · Munchly Foods | Appearance | Appearance | Notifications | Notifications | Profile and settings⟩",
  "profile": "Smart‑Clearance Munchly Foodsmunchly.smartclearance.com Finance & ESG Evidence Batches Vikram SethiSustainability & BRSR · Munchly Foods Profile Profile Sustainability & BRSR Vikram Sethi Sustainability & BRSR · Munchly FoodsGoogle Workspace · vikram.sethi@munchly.in Workspace Munchly Foodsmunchly.smartclearance.comMunchly staff Appearance ThemeLightDarkAuto Notifications LanguageEnglishहिन्दीPush notificationsWeekly digest by email Offers to the trade go out in the language each person picks. Account Switch personTry the journey as someone else in the story Reset demo dataPuts the batch back to the start Sign outBack to munchly.smartclearance.com ⟨Main | Munchly Foods workspace, munchly.smartclearance.com | Vikram Sethi · Sustainability & BRSR · Munchly Foods | Appearance | Appearance | Notifications | Notifications | Profile and settings | Theme | Notification language | Push notifications | Weekly digest⟩",
  "report": "Smart‑Clearance Munchly Foodsmunchly.smartclearance.com Finance & ESG Evidence Batches Vikram SethiSustainability & BRSR · Munchly Foods Finance & ESG QuarterThis batch Finance & ESG Q3 FY27 · Oct to Dec 2026 · one ledger, two readings MF-2409-117 posted · ₹21,152 recovered · 217.6 kg out of landfill · BRSR row addedledger Recovered₹6.3 lakh₹60123456789.30123456789lakh GST credit protected₹79,000₹7012345678990123456789,001234567890012345678900123456789 Kept out of landfill5.750123456789.70123456789 t CO₂e avoided14.251012345678940123456789.2012345678950123456789 tindicative · 2.5 kg a kg Meals served3,70030123456789,701234567890012345678900123456789 A synthetic quarter: the totals are the walkthrough's; the weekly split, the channel mix and the BRSR split below are illustrative. Week 1 is this batch. Recovered against the would-be write-off Illustrative weekly split of the quarter RecoveredWould-be write-off 0₹35k₹70kW1W3W5W7W9W11W13 Channel mix Share of units by where they went · illustrative Kirana scheme: 42%ExpireSoon: 38%Staff sale: 5%Food bank: 12%Write-off: 3% Kirana scheme 42%ExpireSoon 38%Staff sale 5%Food bank 12%Write-off 3% How the tax maths works Destroying stock costs more than the stock. You lose it at cost, reverse the GST input credit under Section 17(5)(h), pay to dispose of it, and owe EPR on the product and pack. Selling it under a tax invoice keeps the credit. That is why every routed batch protects its ITC, even at half the MRP. Donations reverse it. Section 17(5)(h) blocks credit on gifts, and since 1 October 2023 section 17(5)(fa) blocks it on CSR donations too, so a food-bank route costs the credit on every pack. Disposal ₹1.50 a unit, indicativeEPR ₹6 a kg, indicativeCO₂e 2.5 kg per kg, indicative 5.7 tonnes kept out of landfill this quarter, with invoices behind every kilo. That goes straight into the annual report. Vikram · sustainability BRSR Core Principle 6, waste management · the quarter's 5.7 t, split illustrative Export BRSR table CategoryDiverted, kgResoldDonatedDisposedEvidenceFood waste: packaged food past quick-commerce gates4,8404,26058060Tax invoices, ExpireSoon listing IDs, in-app order logs, food-bank receiptsPlastic packaging (EPR)8607709010Packaging weights per SKU, EPR factor, the same invoices ⟨Main | Munchly Foods workspace, munchly.smartclearance.com | Vikram Sethi · Sustainability & BRSR · Munchly Foods | Period | Appearance | Appearance | Notifications | Notifications | Profile and settings | Weekly recovered against would-be write-off | Channel mix | BRSR waste table⟩",
}
`;

